  "verbalization": "Cisapride is shown to bind to multiple cytochrome P450 (CYP) enzymes, including Cyp2a6, Cyp2c8, and Cyp3a4, all of which are involved in steroid hydroxylase activity. This shared pathway suggests a potential mechanism by which Cisapride may influence steroid metabolism. The observed final scores indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Cisapride and Cyp2c19, as it is directly linked through the steroid hydroxylase activity pathway. The mechanism appears to involve Cisapride's ability to inhibit the activity of these enzymes, which in turn affects the metabolism of steroid hormones. The integration of multiple paths highlights a robust, biologically plausible mechanism where Cisapride exerts its effects through the modulation of steroid hydroxylase activity, ultimately influencing Cyp2c19. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Cisapride and Cyp2c19, mediated through the shared role of steroid hydroxylase activity.",
